A reviewer re-derived every number from source and live measurement before
reading the note, with a tokenizer health control first. Eight of eight claims
confirmed in substance; three corrections matter enough to append.

The largest one reverses a recommendation. The note's biggest saving was
fetch-on-demand for the 4,667-token object table. That table is default-ON
because of a measured held-out win -- +0.0720 change_fidelity over 20 paired
games, sign-test p = 0.0192, 13,171s of compute. Removing it to save tokens
would un-buy that result. The structural claim survives and was independently
reproduced (4,691 / 55.5% on seed 0 vs 4,667 / 54% on seed 5900): the object
table IS the largest block. So the target is right and the move is wrong, and
any change there is an A/B rather than an optimisation.

Second: the denominator 84 does not reproduce. Shards give 0 of 83 graded or
0 of 88 delta-bearing; the repo contradicts itself at arc_llm_reinduction.py:39
("0 of 83") versus :1242 ("84 refinement cells"). Destructive holds at either
denominator -- pooled deltas -0.0128 and -0.0598, 8 of 8 partially-correct
engines collapsing to 0.0. Corrected because this project audits denominators.

Third: two ranges are narrow samples. _rle_grid 1,709-1,857 is 2 frames; an
8-game sweep reaches 2,776 on ft09. The 8-78 delta range spliced two encoders.

Appended, not edited, per never-prune.

